# =========================
# Virtual environments
# =========================
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# =========================
# Python cache
# =========================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/

# =========================
# Jupyter
# =========================
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# =========================
# Environment / secrets
# =========================
.env
.env.*
*.env

# =========================
# Data folders - DO NOT UPLOAD
# =========================
data/
reports/
## srcss/ - If you have a src/ folder, you might want to ignore it if it contains sensitive information or if it's not meant to be shared. However, if src/ contains your main codebase, you should consider keeping it in version control. Adjust this based on your project's structure and needs.
# src/

# =========================
# Models / artifacts
# =========================
models/*
!models/runs/
artifacts/

# Provenance/report files under models/runs/ are tracked; model binaries,
# parquet, and logs stay ignored everywhere (including under models/runs/).
models/runs/*
!models/runs/*/
!models/runs/*.json
!models/runs/*.md
models/runs/*/*
!models/runs/*/*.json
!models/runs/*/*.csv
!models/runs/*/*.md

# =========================
# Logs / temp
# =========================
*.log
tmp/
temp/

# =========================
# IDE / OS files
# =========================
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
## obsidian_vault/ - If you are using Obsidian for note-taking and it creates a vault in your project directory, you might want to ignore it to prevent sensitive notes from being uploaded. Adjust this based on your project's structure and needs.
obsidian_vault/
note_books/model_eng/read.ipynb
